WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Speaker 1: Let's talk now about Florida. Florida&nbsp;
is a state where incumbent Republican Senator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:12.060
Marco Rubio is trying to stave off a challenge&nbsp;
from a Democratic congresswoman, Val Demings. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:18.060
I voted in Florida, I would vote for Demings over&nbsp;
Marco Rubio. Marco Rubio appeared on CNN over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.860
weekend. He sounded very, very sick. Hopefully&nbsp;
it's not COVID and just the cold, but he sounded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:29.760
ill and he was confronted about the fact that in&nbsp;
the past he has voted against funding for other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.620
states when they are hit with a national natural&nbsp;
disaster. But now he wants money for Florida&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.540
when it's his state recovering from Hurricane&nbsp;
Ian. Now, to remind everybody in my audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:46.500
I think they all should get the federal funds&nbsp;
for disaster relief. But what we're talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:53.400
about here is hypocrisy. Now, when Dana Bash&nbsp;
confronts Rubio with this hypocrisy, he tries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:59.880
to pull some weird pork thing. And Dana Bash,&nbsp;
good for her, is prepared for it and she calls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.660
it out for the lie that it is. Check this out.
Speaker 5: Senator, you wrote a letter Friday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.940
to the Senate Appropriations Committee asking&nbsp;
for disaster relief dollars for desperately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:14.940
needed resources to rebuild Florida communities.&nbsp;
After Hurricane Sandy hit northeastern states&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:20.700
in 2012. You voted no on a $50 billion relief&nbsp;
package. I know you supported a smaller version,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:26.160
but why should other senators vote for&nbsp;
relief for your state when you didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.620
vote for a package to help theirs? Right.&nbsp;
Oh, I've always voted for hurricane disaster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:35.700
relief. I've even voted for it without pay&nbsp;
force. But I didn't vote for it, Sandy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.120
because they had included things like a&nbsp;
roof for a museum in Washington, D.C.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.500
for fisheries in Alaska. It had been loaded up&nbsp;
with a bunch of things that had nothing to do with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.300
disaster relief. And I wouldn't support disaster&nbsp;
relief efforts. I would never put out there that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.860
we should go use a disaster relief package for&nbsp;
Florida as a way to pay for all kinds of other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:57.480
things people want around the country. So I think&nbsp;
that's the key in moments like this. And Sandy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.960
unfortunately, they loaded it up. They really did&nbsp;
with a bunch of things that had nothing to do with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.940
Sandy. But get ready. I voted for every disaster&nbsp;
relief package, especially that's clean and I'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:09.000
continue to do so when it comes to Florida.&nbsp;
I'll do that again and we'll make sure that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.900
that package is clean and doesn't have stuff for&nbsp;
other people in there. I read the Congressional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:18.180
Research Service report last night. It sounds like&nbsp;
that roof actually was damaged by the hurricane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.700
and what happened in alaska.
Speaker 1: Turns out it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.940
wasn't a random roof, marco.
Speaker 5: The result of another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:29.700
disaster. But in any event, what my question&nbsp;
is about the future. Are you telling me that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:34.800
if hurricane and relief contains anything&nbsp;
that smells like pork, you'll vote? No?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.780
Sure, I'll fight against it. Having pork in it.
Speaker 1: Oh, well, that's a different thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:44.280
You'll fight against it, but you'll vote for&nbsp;
it. In this particular case, this is not unique&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.120
to Rubio, not like in Rubio's defense. I mean,&nbsp;
we're talking about Rubio because it's Florida.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:53.880
He represents Florida. But this is really common&nbsp;
over the last decade on this program, it's been,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:58.380
what, a dozen times, two dozen times that I've&nbsp;
come to you all with peace and love and tears in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:04.680
my eyes. And I've said to you, here is another&nbsp;
elected official from Oklahoma. Oklahoma just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:11.460
got hit with tornadoes, this very same Oklahoma&nbsp;
official when it was Superstorm Sandy affecting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.900
New York and New Jersey. They voted against&nbsp;
it. And now they're saying, give me the money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:22.380
please. We need it for the people. These&nbsp;
are hypocrites and there's dozens of them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:28.140
And it's not unique to Marco Rubio, but Marco&nbsp;
Rubio is the guy running for reelection right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:34.620
now and checking in on the polling there. It's&nbsp;
not great, but it's not terrible. Marco Rubio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:43.740
leading Val Demings on average by 2.8 percentage&nbsp;
points within reach. Within reach. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:51.240
all these guys and I do mean Rubio and DeSantis&nbsp;
all of a sudden they're friendly with Biden and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:56.100
they're all in favor of relief because they&nbsp;
don't want to lose their office because of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.480
disastrous botched reaction to Hurricane&nbsp;
Ian. That's their priority right now.

